{
  "request": {
    "model": "nomic-embed-text:latest",
    "input": [
      "Synthetic nurse note for software testing. No real patient data.\n\nThe commercial driver attends after a long shift with a folder containing a current signed letter, older screening paperwork and a handwritten personal account, and the nurse reconstructs the chronology before recording the present findings; differences between the records are described explicitly rather than resolved by treating the newest-looking photocopy as automatically authoritative.\n\nThe driver recalls a short gap in a radio conversation while seated after unloading, but a colleague says he remained responsive and might simply have been distracted by paperwork; the nurse cannot confirm loss of consciousness or a blackout from the conflicting accounts, a pulse reading taken later does not resolve awareness during the episode, and the physician has requested further history rather than diagnosing a specific cause.\n\nThe usual work involves coupling trailers, checking mirrors, interpreting radio messages and responding to pedestrians in a loading area, with breaks that can be delayed when deliveries run late; the driver explains which difficulty occurred while stationary and which was noticed during ordinary duties, rather than claiming that quiet conversation in the clinic reproduces every task in the cab.\n\nThe record is prepared for the reviewing clinician with the sequence of events and the provenance of the available findings intact, because the employer summary and the driver's account answer different questions; a completed test is retained as such, but an unresolved detail is not filled in from a family member's history or from an earlier document with different testing conditions.\n"
    ],
    "truncate": false
  },
  "provider_called": true,
  "status": "completed",
